From: LuneOS <webos-ports@googlegroups.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Exit non-zero on an unknown extent target type

The unknown-target-type arm of the switch does "return false" from main(),
which is an int, so false converts to 0 and the process reports success. The
caller then does

    dmsetup create --concise "$(parse-android-dynparts ...)"

with a truncated table and no indication anything went wrong, which is a
considerably worse failure than exiting non-zero would be.

Every other error path in main() returns 1; make this one match.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/main.cpp
+++ b/main.cpp
@@ -130,7 +130,7 @@
         default:
           cerr << "Unknown target type in metadata: " << extent.target_type
                << endl;
-          return false;
+          return 1;
       }
       sector += extent.num_sectors;
     }
